# requant_parity -- table parity: no fault, no flag; the fault on a written entry 0 under in_valid flags the next cycle
# requant at COLS = 4 (PW = 32, MW = 16), every input free, tbl_fault_inject included: tbl_perr_sticky is exactly "the
# fault met a written entry 0 during in_valid since err_clear" -- with the fault off it never rises, whatever the
# unwritten entries hold; with it, it is 1 one cycle later and holds until err_clear. Full proof by k-induction
# (drop 0.41); requant_parity_fv.sv holds the harness. Drop 0.43: after a cycle with the block's clock enable low, no
# valid, written entry or sticky has changed (the gate's formal model neo_icg_formal.sv, ungated: gating it is invisible).
[options]
mode prove
depth 4

[engines]
smtbmc yices

[script]
plugin -i slang
read_slang -DFORMAL --top requant_parity_fv neo_icg_formal.sv requant.sv requant_parity_fv.sv
prep -top requant_parity_fv

[files]
formal/neo_icg_formal.sv
rtl/requant.sv
formal/requant_parity_fv.sv
